@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Deploy Orchestration
  "Plans and executes build-directory rsync deploys with pre-flight diff and post-run summary inputs."

  Provides:
    - deploy.Rsync @source("symbol:Rsync")
    - deploy.Service @source("symbol:Service")
    - deploy.NewService @source("symbol:NewService")
    - deploy.DeployOptions @source("symbol:DeployOptions")
    - deploy.Result @source("symbol:Result")
    - deploy.Service.Run
    - deploy.Service.Execute @source("symbol:Execute")
    - deploy.UpToDate @source("symbol:UpToDate")

  Consumes:
    - config.Target
    - remote.CompareDryRunRequest
    - remote.RsyncRequest
    - deploy.Planner
    - deploy.Plan

  Invariants:
    - Run MUST plan with rsync dry-run before any real transfer
    - Run MUST skip rsync upload when DryRun is true or the plan is already up to date
    - Deploy MUST use the same source and destination paths as the planner

  OutOfScope:
    - CLI rendering and confirmation prompts (owned by internal/cli)
    - mason init scaffolding (future M-062)

  Scenario (happy-path): Dry-run plan
    Given DryRun is true
    When Run executes
    Then it returns the plan without uploading bytes

  Scenario (happy-path): Deploy changes
    Given a plan with files to send
    When Run executes without DryRun
    Then rsync upload runs and Result marks Deployed true

  Scenario (happy-path): Already up to date
    Given a plan with zero changes
    When Run executes
    Then no rsync upload runs and UpToDate is true

  Scenario (negative): Missing deploy config
    Given a target without deploy paths
    When Run executes
    Then it returns an error before transfer
